From blackwel at fas.harvard.edu  Mon Jan 25 17:07:41 2010
From: blackwel at fas.harvard.edu (Matt Blackwell)
Date: Mon, 25 Jan 2010 17:07:41 -0500
Subject: [amelia] separating NAs and DKs in Amelia analysis?
In-Reply-To: <3142359A-055A-4CAE-9BD7-EF9CE7653839@calpoly.edu>
References: <3142359A-055A-4CAE-9BD7-EF9CE7653839@calpoly.edu>
Message-ID: <839691711001251407k42d5452ap7f91469cbf6c6893@mail.gmail.com>

Hi Shanruo,

If you don't want to include the NAs in the analysis at all, you can
remove them from the data and then run the imputation model. You could
also leave them in the imputation, but then change their imputations
back NA manually.

Note that any cell that needs to be imputed must be coded as "NA" (the
missing value code for R). An alternative method would be to code all
NAs as another category of the variable which is observed. Only DKs
would then be missing.

Hope that helps,
matt.

